From 7781d37838306edf329746654bdb37f86a4747e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:11:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: a missing system bus is not a warning

set_accountsservice_user_bg() mirrors the backdrop into AccountsService
(for a greeter) over the system bus. A session without AccountsService
is logged at debug level only, but a session without a system bus at all
-- a desktop with only a session bus, as on Phoenix-RTOS -- printed
"Failed to get system bus" as a warning on every start. Both mean the
same thing here: there is nobody to tell. Log it at debug level too.
---
 src/xfce-desktop.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/xfce-desktop.c b/src/xfce-desktop.c
index 502d2f7..f377293 100644
--- a/src/xfce-desktop.c
+++ b/src/xfce-desktop.c
@@ -206,7 +206,9 @@ set_accountsservice_user_bg(const gchar *background)
 
     bus = g_bus_get_sync (G_BUS_TYPE_SYSTEM, NULL, &error);
     if (bus == NULL) {
-        g_warning ("Failed to get system bus: %s", error->message);
+        // As when AccountsService is not running (below): the user's background
+        // is then just not mirrored there, which is no reason to warn
+        DBG("Failed to get system bus: %s", error->message);
         g_error_free (error);
         return;
     }
-- 
